(>> 2.1 The Cytoskeletal Architecture: Three Distinct Filament Systems) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(The eukaryotic cytoplasm is structured by a dynamic polymeric filament network essential) Tj
T*
(for mechanical integrity, cell division, organellar positioning, and intracellular) Tj
T*
(trafficking.) Tj
T*
(* Microtubules: Hollow, cylindrical polymers of 25 nm outer diameter composed of 13) Tj
T*
(parallel protofilaments. Each protofilament is a linear polymer of alpha- and) Tj
T*
(beta-tubulin heterodimers stacked head-to-tail, conferring structural polarity \(plus) Tj
T*
(end terminates with beta-tubulin; minus end terminates with alpha-tubulin\).) Tj
T*
(Microtubules originate from Microtubule Organizing Centers \(MTOCs/Centrosomes\) where) Tj
T*
(gamma-tubulin ring complexes \(gamma-TuRC\) nucleate minus ends.) Tj
T*
(* Dynamic Instability: Microtubules alternate stochastically between slow growth) Tj
T*
(\(polymerization\) and rapid catastrophe \(depolymerization\). Beta-tubulin binds GTP;) Tj
T*
(when incorporated at the growing plus end, GTP is hydrolyzed to GDP. If) Tj
T*
(polymerization rate exceeds hydrolysis, a stabilizing 'GTP Cap' is maintained. Loss) Tj
T*
(of the GTP cap triggers conformational strain within the lattice, causing outward) Tj
T*
(curling of protofilaments and rapid catastrophic disassembly. Rescue occurs when a) Tj
T*
(new GTP cap re-forms.) Tj
T*
(* Microfilaments \(Actin Filaments\): Two-stranded helical polymers of globular actin) Tj
T*
(\(G-actin\) with a diameter of 7 nm. Structurally polar with a barbed \(plus\) end and) Tj
T*
(pointed \(minus\) end. Actin filaments undergo 'treadmilling' at steady state:) Tj
T*
(G-actin-ATP monomers add preferentially to the barbed end \(lower critical) Tj
T*
(concentration, Cc = 0.12 microM\) while G-actin-ADP dissociates from the pointed end) Tj
T*
(\(higher Cc = 0.6 microM\). Regulated by actin-binding proteins: profilin \(promotes) Tj
T*
(ADP-to-ATP exchange\), cofilin \(severs ADP-actin filaments\), and Arp2/3 complex) Tj
T*
(\(nucleates 70-degree branched actin networks\).) Tj
T*
(* Intermediate Filaments: Non-polar, 10 nm ropelike fibers conferring mechanical) Tj
T*
(tensile strength. Composed of cell-type specific fibrous proteins: keratins) Tj
T*
(\(epithelia\), vimentin \(mesenchymal cells\), neurofilaments \(neurons\), and nuclear) Tj
T*
(lamins \(nucleoplasm\). Subunits form antiparallel staggered tetramers, precluding) Tj
T*
(directional polarity.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 2.2 Molecular Motor Proteins) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Kinesins: Plus-end-directed microtubule motors that mediate anterograde transport) Tj
T*
(\(from centrosome toward cell periphery\). Move processively in discrete 8 nm steps) Tj
T*
(utilizing ATP hydrolysis by two globular motor heads in a coordinated hand-over-hand) Tj
T*
(mechanism.) Tj
T*
(* Dyneins: Minus-end-directed microtubule motors mediating retrograde transport) Tj
T*
(\(toward centrosome\). Cytoplasmic dynein is a massive multisubunit complex \(1.2 MDa\)) Tj
T*
(requiring the dynactin cofactor complex to bind cargo vesicles. Axonemal dynein) Tj
T*
