/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 2.4 Vesicular Transport Machinery: Coats and SNAREs) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* COPII-Coated Vesicles: Mediate anterograde transport from ER to ER-Golgi) Tj
T*
(intermediate compartment \(ERGIC\) and cis-Golgi. Coat assembly is initiated by Sar1) Tj
T*
(GTPase, which recruits Sec23-Sec24 inner cargo-adaptor heterodimers followed by) Tj
T*
(Sec13-Sec31 outer cage complexes.) Tj
T*
(* COPI-Coated Vesicles: Mediate retrograde retrieval transport from Golgi back to ER.) Tj
T*
(Recruited by Arf1 GTPase. Recognizes C-terminal retrieval signals: KDEL on soluble) Tj
T*
(luminal ER proteins \(via KDEL receptor\) and KKXX on transmembrane proteins.) Tj
T*
(* Clathrin-Coated Vesicles: Mediate transport from TGN to endosomes/lysosomes and) Tj
T*
(from plasma membrane inward during endocytosis. Mannose-6-phosphate \(M6P\) tags on) Tj
T*
(lysosomal enzymes are recognized by M6P receptors in TGN and incorporated into) Tj
T*
(clathrin coats via GGA and AP1 adaptors.) Tj
T*
(* SNARE-Mediated Fusion: Vesicle targeting specificity is governed by Rab family) Tj
T*
(small GTPases and tethering complexes. Fusion is executed by SNAREs: one v-SNARE) Tj
T*
(\(e.g., synaptobrevin\) on vesicle pairs with three t-SNARE helices \(e.g., syntaxin and) Tj
T*
(SNAP-25\) on target membrane to assemble a four-helix trans-SNARE bundle) Tj
T*
(\(coiled-coil\). Bundle zippering overcomes electrostatic repulsion, forcing lipid) Tj
T*
(bilayer hemifusion and complete fusion. Disassembly of the stable cis-SNARE complex) Tj
