/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Context: Taxol \(paclitaxel\) and Vinca alkaloids \(vincristine, vinblastine\) both) Tj
T*
(disrupt the microtubule cytoskeleton to halt cancer cell proliferation, yet act through) Tj
T*
(opposite biophysical mechanisms. Detail their molecular targets, cellular consequences,) Tj
T*
(and therapeutic rationale.) Tj
T*
(Molecular Target 1 \(Taxol\): Paclitaxel binds stoichiometrically to the interior surface) Tj
T*
(of the beta-tubulin subunit within the microtubule wall. It stabilizes lateral) Tj
T*
(protofilament interactions, suppresses dynamic instability, and prevents microtubule) Tj
T*
(depolymerization even in the absence of GTP. Mitotic spindles become frozen and cannot) Tj
T*
(generate tension required to separate sister chromatids.) Tj
T*
(Molecular Target 2 \(Vinca Alkaloids\): Vincristine binds to tubulin heterodimers at the) Tj
T*
(interface between alpha and beta subunits, inhibiting polymerization at high) Tj
T*
(concentrations and inducing spiral aggregate formation. Microtubules depolymerize and) Tj
T*
(mitotic spindles fail to assemble.) Tj
T*
(Cellular Outcome: In both cases, kinetochores remain unattached or lack tension. The) Tj
T*
(Mad2/BubR1 spindle assembly checkpoint \(SAC\) remains persistently active, sequestering) Tj
T*
(Cdc20 and inhibiting the Anaphase-Promoting Complex/Cyclosome \(APC/C\). Cells arrest in) Tj
T*
(prometaphase and activate mitochondria-dependent intrinsic apoptosis.) Tj
T*
(Conclusion: Manipulating microtubule catastrophe/assembly kinetics selectively) Tj
T*
(eradicates rapidly dividing neoplasias by triggering SAC-mediated mitotic catastrophe.) Tj
T*
