(Problem Context: Describe the molecular etiology, biochemical defect, and cellular) Tj
T*
(phenotype of I-Cell Disease, an autosomal recessive lysosomal storage disorder.) Tj
T*
(Normal Targeting Pathway: In the cis-Golgi, lysosomal hydrolases are recognized by) Tj
T*
(UDP-N-acetylglucosamine:lysosomal-enzyme N-acetylglucosamine-1-phosphotransferase) Tj
T*
(\(GlcNAc phosphotransferase\). It recognizes a specific 3D protein conformation epitope) Tj
T*
(\(signal patch\) and transfers GlcNAc-1-phosphate to terminal mannoses of N-linked) Tj
T*
(glycans. In the trans-Golgi, phosphodiesterase removes GlcNAc, leaving exposed) Tj
T*
(Mannose-6-Phosphate \(M6P\) residues that bind M6P receptors for clathrin-mediated) Tj
T*
(lysosomal packaging.) Tj
T*
(Biochemical Lesion in I-Cell Disease: Loss-of-function mutation in the GNPTAB gene) Tj
T*
(encoding the alpha/beta subunits of GlcNAc phosphotransferase. Lysosomal enzymes fail to) Tj
T*
(acquire the M6P targeting signal.) Tj
T*
(Pathological Outcome: Unmodified acid hydrolases are not sorted into transport vesicles) Tj
T*
(at the TGN. Instead, they are routed through the default constitutive secretory pathway) Tj
T*
(and dumped into the extracellular bloodstream.) Tj
T*
(Phenotype: Lysosomes lack essential degradation enzymes and become engorged with) Tj
T*
