(Thermodynamic Work Calculation:) Tj
T*
(Mechanical Work \(W\) = Force * Distance = F * d) Tj
T*
(W = \(6 * 10^-12 N\) * \(8.2 * 10^-9 m\) = 4.92 * 10^-20 Joules per step.) Tj
T*
(Available Chemical Free Energy from ATP Hydrolysis:) Tj
T*
(delta G_ATP under cellular conditions = -50 kJ/mol = \(50,000 J\) / \(6.022 * 10^23\) = 8.30) Tj
T*
(* 10^-20 Joules per molecule.) Tj
T*
(Thermodynamic Efficiency \(eta\):) Tj
T*
(eta = \(Mechanical Work Done / Chemical Energy Consumed\) * 100) Tj
T*
(eta = \(4.92 * 10^-20 J / 8.30 * 10^-20 J\) * 100 = 59.3%.) Tj
T*
(Conclusion: Kinesin operates at ~60% thermodynamic efficiency, vastly surpassing) Tj
